From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 13:19:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] SetupWizard: leave mobile data alone

onCreate() calls setMobileDataEnabled(this, false) unconditionally for the owner, and nothing ever
turns it back on: finishSetupWizard() sets DEVICE_PROVISIONED and USER_SETUP_COMPLETE but not this,
and there is no mobile-data page anywhere in the wizard. The only call site in the whole app passes
false.

The result is a device that finishes setup with mobile data off and no indication why, on a fresh
install where the user has no other way to know. It also makes the wizard itself unusable without
Wi-Fi, and DataSettingsManager ignores the user setting entirely while DEVICE_PROVISIONED is 0, so
the value written here is not even the one consulted during setup.

Drop the call and inherit whatever the platform default is.

---
 src/org/lineageos/setupwizard/SetupWizardApp.java | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/org/lineageos/setupwizard/SetupWizardApp.java b/src/org/lineageos/setupwizard/SetupWizardApp.java
index 51d65af..60b327c 100644
--- a/src/org/lineageos/setupwizard/SetupWizardApp.java
+++ b/src/org/lineageos/setupwizard/SetupWizardApp.java
@@ -95,9 +95,6 @@ public class SetupWizardApp extends Application {
         NetworkMonitor.initInstance(this);
         PhoneMonitor.initInstance(this);
         SetupWizardUtils.disableComponentsForMissingFeatures(this);
-        if (SetupWizardUtils.isOwner()) {
-            SetupWizardUtils.setMobileDataEnabled(this, false);
-        }
         sStatusBarManager = SetupWizardUtils.disableStatusBar(this);
         mHandler.postDelayed(mRadioTimeoutRunnable, SetupWizardApp.RADIO_READY_TIMEOUT);
     }
